### Summary

The selection guard in the row click handler fixes the earlier drag-select issue, and I found no defects in the production change. One minor test-hygiene note: the `getSelection` spy is restored inline, so a failing assertion would leak the mock into later tests.

<details><summary>What the change connects to (1 closed, 0 open)</summary>

Questions the reviewer answered about what this change does to the running product. The engine checked that the cited lines exist, not that the answers are true.

**Closed, with the lines they rest on**
- Click on a selectable finding row now skips the toggle when the page has a non-empty text selection (`apps/kaipu-record/src/renderer/src/features/library/reconcile/reconcile-dialog.tsx:216`) — Dragging over a name to copy it no longer unticks the row. A plain click collapses any prior selection on mousedown, so a normal click still toggles. If it fails: window.getSelection() can return null; optional chaining makes that fall through to the toggle. No async work, so there is no rejection or timeout path. Evidence: `apps/kaipu-record/src/renderer/src/features/library/reconcile/reconcile-dialog.tsx:211-220`, `apps/kaipu-record/src/renderer/src/features/library/reconcile/reconcile.test.tsx:353-378`.

